  "docTitle": "IoT Telemetry & Real-time Heatmaps - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design high-volume device and location telemetry: smart meters to a usage dashboard, continent-wide temperature heatmaps, machine-sensor alerts with an acknowledge/resolve state machine, and Uber's real-time driver-density heatmap. MQTT to Kafka, H3 bucketing, Flink windows, a time-series DB with downsampling, Redis pub/sub to WebSockets.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span><span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span><span class=\"chip company\">Uber</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>IoT Telemetry &amp; Real-time Heatmaps</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Millions of small devices (smart meters, temperature sensors, factory machines, driver phones) keep saying \"here is my reading\". Design the system that swallows that stream, paints a live heatmap and a history chart, and raises one clean alert when something goes out of range - and be ready to explain, line by line, how the update actually reaches the browser.</p>\n      "
  },
